- Border: a subtle neutral

Treat the palette as a coordinated design system, not a requirement to display all five colors equally.

Use the dark primary color for navigation, headings, and important structural elements. Use teal for primary actions and active states. Reserve yellow, orange, and coral for meaningful highlights, warnings, priorities, and status indicators.

Verify text contrast and never rely on color alone to communicate task status or validation errors.

