## 20. FINAL EXECUTION RULE

Prioritize functional correctness, architectural consistency, accessibility, and visual quality equally.

Use the provided product specification to determine what TaskDo must do. Use these instructions to determine how its frontend should be designed and implemented.

Make reasonable implementation decisions without repeatedly asking questions that can be resolved by inspecting the repository or following the documented architecture.

When a requirement cannot be completed because a backend, credential, external service, or missing dependency is unavailable, implement the appropriate frontend boundary and clearly document the remaining requirement.

At completion, report:

1. What was implemented.
2. Which application workflows are functional.
3. Which integrations require external configuration.
4. Which tests and build commands were executed.
5. Any remaining limitations or known issues.

Never claim that a feature, test, migration, or deployment works unless it has actually been implemented and verified.